I have successfully fixed the bug by modifying `packages/core/src/config/storage.ts` so that `getProjectTempTrackerDir()` respects the `sessionId` when it is provided. I also implemented targeted unit tests to verify the correct behavior.

### Summary of Changes

* **Implementation Fix:**
  * Updated **`getProjectTempTrackerDir()`** in [storage.ts](file:///usr/local/google/home/joneba/ssr-prototype/gcli-intern-project/tools/caretaker-agent/evals/pr-generation/run_outputs/small_triaged_3.5_flash/agent_environments/gemini_cli_22198/tmp/pr/gemini-cli/packages/core/src/config/storage.ts) to check if `this.sessionId` exists.
  * If `this.sessionId` exists, it returns `path.join(this.getProjectTempDir(), this.sessionId, 'tracker')`.
  * Otherwise, it defaults to returning `path.join(this.getProjectTempDir(), 'tracker')`.

* **Testing Additions:**
  * Added two new unit tests in [storage.test.ts](file:///usr/local/google/home/joneba/ssr-prototype/gcli-intern-project/tools/caretaker-agent/evals/pr-generation/run_outputs/small_triaged_3.5_flash/agent_environments/gemini_cli_22198/tmp/pr/gemini-cli/packages/core/src/config/storage.test.ts):
    1. Verifies that calling `getProjectTempTrackerDir()` without a session ID returns `path.join(tempDir, 'tracker')`.
    2. Verifies that calling `getProjectTempTrackerDir()` with a session ID returns `path.join(tempDir, sessionId, 'tracker')`.

---

